{title: Another King}
{subtitle: Acts 17:5–7; 17:6–8; 17:9; Romans 16:21}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] |
| [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]They rounded up the s[Dm]coundrels
From the marketplace street
[Bb]Formed a wild and an[F]gry mob
In the city's [C]heat
They stormed the house at night
[Dm]To find the two men
[Bb]But they could not find them [F]there
So the search was [C]done
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They [Dm]dragged Jason to the court
Along with [Bb]some brothers
[F]Shouting out their accusation
[C]With their loud reports
[Dm]These men turned the world up[Bb]side down
Now they have [F]come here
Jason has taken them [C]in
The anger is [Dm]clear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They act against the decrees
Of Caesar the great
[Bb]Saying there is anoth[F]er king
With a different [C]fate
The crowd was thrown into con[Dm]fusion
The officials con[Bb]fused
But Jason stood his [F]ground
In this dangerous [C]news
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
So they took [Dm]bail from Jason
And [Bb]the others too
And re[F]leased them from the court
As the [C]day broke through
The cost [Dm]was paid for the gospel
The [Bb]loss was his share
Yet he [F]welcomed them freely
[C]With his open [Dm]door [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Jason sends his greetings
[C]A kinsman of [Dm]Paul
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
